  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: configuration injection in configparser via a carriage\n     return in an attacker-controlled written value\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-0864.patch: in Lib/configparser.py, normalize\n       CR and CRLF to LF before indenting continuation lines in\n       RawConfigParser._write_section(), so a bare carriage return inside a\n       written value can no longer round-trip into an unindented line that\n       the parser reads back as a separate \"key = value\" pair. Backport of\n       upstream commit 5858e42c539d (gh-143927 / GH-143929) via the 3.10\n       backport 12dcbd74d356; applies to 3.7.3 with line offsets only.\n       Bundles the upstream regression test test_crlf_normalization\n       (test_configparser.py).\n     - CVE-2026-0864",
